(Vehicle Diagnostics Primer \(synthetic sample\)) '
() '
(Controller Area Network \(CAN\) is a serial bus that lets electronic control units in a) '
(vehicle exchange messages without a central host. Each message has an identifier that) '
(sets its priority, and a node that loses arbitration waits and retries.) '
() '
(A classical CAN frame carries up to eight data bytes. Typical bus speeds are 125) '
(kbit/s for body electronics and 500 kbit/s for powertrain. Two twisted wires, CAN) '
(high and CAN low, carry a differential signal, and a 120 ohm terminating resistor) '
(sits at each end of the bus.) '
() '
(When a node detects an error it sends an error frame. A node with repeated errors) '
(moves to the error passive state and finally goes bus off, so that one faulty unit) '
(cannot block the whole network.) '
ET
endstream
endobj
